      "source": [
        "### Accessing elements in a list\n",
        "In Python, you can access elements in a list by using indexing, which allows you to retrieve items based on their position within the list.\n",
        "\n",
        "* Positive indices start at 0 and count from left to right. For example, the first item in a list is at index 0, the second at index 1, and so on.\n",
        "\n",
        "* Negative indices start from the end of the list and count backward. The last item is at index -1, the second-to-last at -2, and so forth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 48,
