      "metadata": {
        "id": "a88d9477"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Sorting\n",
        "\n",
        "You can sort a list using the sort() method or the sorted() function."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "696c3988",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "696c3988"
      },
      "source": [
        "sort(): Sorts the list in place and doesn’t return a new list."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 73,
      "id": "fcf87dbf",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fcf87dbf",
        "outputId": "3e14b460-556b-4746-969e-87167bdffc2a",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "None\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "sorted_number =  number.sort()\n",
        "print(sorted_number)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8f963fa6",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8f963fa6"
      },
      "source": [
        "sorted(): Returns a new sorted list, leaving the original list unchanged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 74,
      "id": "3902fec1",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3902fec1",
        "outputId": "d5d697a3-7a7a-4757-f836-3556b6409ea3",
