        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[98, 87, 78, 78, 65, 47, 45, 3, 2, 1]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "sorted_number = sorted(number, reverse=True) # reverse=True means sort from largest to smallest\n",
        "print(sorted_number)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e41e6d13",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e41e6d13"
      },
      "source": [
        "<a name='7-2'></a>\n",
        "\n",
        "### 7.2 Tuples\n",
        "Tuples are like lists, but they're immutable. This means that once you create a tuple, you can't change the items in it. They're like sealed boxes, once they're packed, they can't be unpacked and repacked. Tuples are commonly used for data that shouldn’t be changed, like geographic coordinates etc."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4215064f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4215064f"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Creating a Tuple\n",
        "\n",
        "Tuples are created using parentheses ( () )."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 75,
      "id": "3ad83ea3",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3ad83ea3",
        "outputId": "5992ac83-4b22-4bdd-872d-7cfc391f4291",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "(10, 23)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "tuple1 = (10, 23)\n",
        "print(tuple1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fcc989a2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fcc989a2"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Accessing Elements\n",
        "\n",
        "Elements in a tuple can be accessed by index just like in a list."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 76,
      "id": "1c6dc906",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1c6dc906",
        "outputId": "d331ae26-24e6-40ff-ea48-8f508647e90a",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "10\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "print(tuple1[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1f3c300d",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1f3c300d"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Immutability\n",
        "\n",
        "Once created, you cannot add, remove, or change items in a tuple."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 77,
      "id": "3cc6453a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3cc6453a"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# This will raise an error\n",
        "# tuple1[0] = 15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5bd6d792",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5bd6d792"
      },
      "source": [
        "<a name='7-3'></a>\n",
        "\n",
        "### 7.3 Dictionaries\n",
        "\n",
        "A dictionary is a collection of key-value pairs. Unlike lists or tuples, dictionaries are unordered. They are useful for storing data that has a meaningful label for each value, like names and ages or usernames and email addresses. Dictionaries are incredibly useful for mapping information and handling data that requires a label."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4d48a92d",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4d48a92d"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Creating a Dictionary\n",
        "\n",
        "Dictionaries are created using curly braces ( {} ) with each pair defined as key: value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 78,
      "id": "cbbac34e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cbbac34e",
        "outputId": "4977e955-21fe-4e0a-db9f-86587f18dafa",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{'name': 'Hart'}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "person = {\"name\": \"Hart\"}  # Key: \"name\", Value: \"Hart\"\n",
        "print(person)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8bcf2dcc",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8bcf2dcc"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Key Features of Dictionaries\n",
        "\n",
        "* Accessing Values: You can get a value by referring to its key inside square brackets [ ]."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 79,
      "id": "f99c557a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f99c557a",
        "outputId": "a4efb093-dc76-4f0d-eabc-22747f50850e",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{'Name': 'Hart', 'Age': 30, 'City': 'Lagos'}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "person = {\"Name\": \"Hart\",\"Age\": 30,\"City\": \"Lagos\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "print(person)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 80,
      "id": "13dae64a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "13dae64a",
        "outputId": "9268efa9-f181-40ac-d2dc-6fbe6e1eccca",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "30\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Get age of Alice\n",
        "print(person[\"Age\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fdd2b999",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fdd2b999"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Adding or Updating Entries: You can add a new key-value pair or update an existing one by specifying the key and assigning a value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 81,
      "id": "b5a32a81",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b5a32a81",
        "outputId": "5aa93f09-4f93-4e2b-ac60-94f23ec43912",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{'Name': 'Hart', 'Age': 30, 'City': 'Lagos', '': 34}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Adding a new person\n",
        "person[\"\"] = 34\n",
        "print(person)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 82,
      "id": "bc638c26",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bc638c26",
        "outputId": "d9cc1fe1-78ea-4578-c85c-a5513a184af0",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{'Name': 'Bassey', 'Age': 30, 'City': 'Lagos', '': 34}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Update name\n",
        "person[\"Name\"] = \"Bassey\"\n",
        "print(person)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "91ba0469",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "91ba0469"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Removing Entries: You can remove an entry using the del statement or the .pop() method."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 83,
      "id": "ae3f37b5",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ae3f37b5",
        "outputId": "39d7dd5d-6b7d-4dfa-c009-55414fe95fcf",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{'Name': 'Bassey', 'Age': 30, '': 34}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Remove City from the dictionary\n",
        "del person[\"City\"]\n",
        "print(person)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "436eb449",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "436eb449"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Checking if a Key Exists: Use the in keyword to check if a key exists."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 84,
      "id": "ad3e414c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ad3e414c",
        "outputId": "14a02aa2-8548-4b4f-ca66-e0da38fba11c",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Name is recorded.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "if \"Name\" in person:\n",
        "    print(\"Name is recorded.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d4aeb65a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d4aeb65a"
      },
      "source": [
        "Dictionaries are ideal for representing structured data where each item has a unique identifier (key). They’re especially useful in scenarios where you need to look up information quickly by a specific label, like usernames with associated email addresses or product IDs with descriptions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "3c42a607",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3c42a607"
      },
      "source": [
        "<a name='7-4'></a>\n",
        "\n",
        "### 7.4 Sets\n",
        "A set is an unordered collection of unique items, meaning it automatically removes duplicates. Sets are useful for tasks involving uniqueness and membership checks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5c543cec",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5c543cec"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Creating a Set\n",
        "\n",
        "Sets are created using curly braces ({}), similar to dictionaries, but without key-value pairs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 85,
      "id": "f0b541c5",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f0b541c5",
        "outputId": "61d0f0d1-9786-4134-a218-9f0224b5152e",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "my_set = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\n",
        "print(my_set)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5cd416e3",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5cd416e3"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Unique Properties\n",
        "\n",
        "Sets automatically eliminate duplicate values:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 86,
      "id": "43e55dce",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "43e55dce",
        "outputId": "63210220-966e-410e-e040-4460dd432b9b",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{1, 2, 3, 4}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "numbers = {1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4} #duplicate values are eliminated\n",
        "print(numbers)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "0f1155eb",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0f1155eb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Basic Set Methods"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "56190ef4",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "56190ef4"
      },
      "source": [
        "* add(): Adds an item to the set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 87,
      "id": "5d34b451",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5d34b451",
        "outputId": "b8cfbb95-d4bc-40b2-9d61-d689c8b6a170",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{1, 2, 3, 4, 6}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "numbers.add(6)\n",
        "print(numbers)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fd94131b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fd94131b"
      },
      "source": [
        "* remove(): Removes an item from the set. Raises an error if the item is not found."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 88,
      "id": "5565bccf",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5565bccf",
        "outputId": "276cc494-64e8-443b-efc8-89ce23f40dee",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{1, 2, 3, 6}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "numbers.remove(4)\n",
        "print(numbers)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1fd45afc",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1fd45afc"
      },
      "source": [
        "* union(): Combines two sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 89,
      "id": "8098273f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8098273f",
        "outputId": "b6710eba-512f-465f-c338-3a46c9eec738",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "set1 = {1, 2, 3}\n",
        "set2 = {3, 4, 5}\n",
        "combined = set1.union(set2)\n",
        "print(combined)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "9ce1ee40",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9ce1ee40"
      },
      "source": [
        "* intersection(): Finds common items between two sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 90,
      "id": "ab0f5c33",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ab0f5c33",
        "outputId": "c6706047-9e68-41ec-fd85-c6557d31ab58",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "{3}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "common = set1.intersection(set2)\n",
        "print(common)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8186d1e2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8186d1e2"
      },
      "source": [
        "<a name='8'></a>\n",
        "\n",
        "# 8. Functions\n",
        "Functions are reusable pieces of code that allow you to perform specific tasks. They simplify code, make it reusable, and help organize your code into logical sections. Functions are essential in programming, especially in large projects, as they make code modular and easier to debug."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fa6b5649",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fa6b5649"
      },
      "source": [
        "<a name='8-1'></a>\n",
        "\n",
        "### 8.1 Defining Functions\n",
        "\n",
        "You define a function in Python using the \" def \" keyword. The basic syntax looks like this:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 91,
      "id": "c06e7220",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c06e7220"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def function_name():    # Function header\n",
        "    # Function body (indented)\n",
        "    print(\"This is inside the function\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 92,
      "id": "2616ab48",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2616ab48",
        "outputId": "2bb1e930-9cd4-422f-f99c-ce2eac4723e2",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "This is inside the function\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "function_name()"
      ]
    },
    {
